# Architecture

Study [ACreTeam/ac-decomp](https://github.com/ACreTeam/ac-decomp) for **behavior**. Reimplement with Godot systems. Never copy C structure, `Common_Get` blobs, or mechanical GDScript translations of decomp files.

- **Data:** `Resource` classes under `scripts/data/`, instances as `.tres` under `data/`.
- **Presentation:** scenes under `scenes/`.
- **Behavior:** systems under `scripts/systems/` (autoloads only when a system exists and is shared).
- **Scene-first:** build fixed layout in the editor (`.tscn`, nested `instance=`). Use runtime `instantiate()` only for procedural / ephemeral content, and then place authored packed scenes—do not construct rooms, HUD, or props from meshes in GDScript when a scene would work.
- Prefer composition over inheritance. Keep systems independently testable.
- Use placeholders until the system works. Do not import original game assets.
- Do not add a feature because the decomp has it. See `docs/scope.md`.
- Build vertical slices that stay playable. No months of infrastructure before an in-game test.
- Full notes: `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/decomp-mapping.md`.
